WEBVTT

00:06.423 --> 00:08.425
[theme music playing]

00:29.154 --> 00:30.739
[line ringing]

00:42.042 --> 00:46.963
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

00:52.510 --> 00:53.511
Let's go.

00:55.972 --> 00:56.848
[phone vibrating]

00:56.931 --> 00:58.850
MEMORIAL GATE

01:02.020 --> 01:04.147
Chief, I'm sorry. Excuse me for a moment.

01:06.066 --> 01:07.233
[phone vibrating]

01:08.693 --> 01:09.903
Yes, what is it?

01:09.986 --> 01:12.030
[nurse] This is
Yongju Silver Care Hospital.

01:12.113 --> 01:14.574
We can't locate Mr. Na Jin-cheol.

01:14.657 --> 01:18.161
Your number was listed
as the emergency contact, so I called you.

01:18.244 --> 01:20.246
Okay, I'll be right there.

01:20.330 --> 01:21.247
[line disconnects]

01:21.331 --> 01:22.582
[somber music playing]

01:22.665 --> 01:24.125
What's the matter?

01:25.668 --> 01:28.379
There seems to be an issue
with my father-in-law.

01:28.463 --> 01:30.507
[press secretary] Oh no.
Then you should hurry.

01:30.590 --> 01:34.302
Use my official vehicle.
They'll get you there quickly and safely.

01:34.385 --> 01:35.261
[sighs]

01:37.388 --> 01:39.432
[siren blaring]

01:54.447 --> 01:55.657
- [Hee-joo coughs]
- Oh, dear.

01:55.740 --> 01:56.908
Are you okay?

01:56.991 --> 01:57.992
[breathing heavily]

02:02.330 --> 02:04.082
- [Hee-joo sobbing]
- [sirens approaching]

02:04.916 --> 02:05.750
What?

02:07.252 --> 02:09.838
Why are they coming towards us?

02:10.421 --> 02:12.423
- Did we do something wrong?
- No way!

02:12.507 --> 02:13.591
We didn't do anything.

02:21.391 --> 02:23.393
[gripping music playing]

02:32.485 --> 02:33.403
Oh.

02:36.531 --> 02:38.908
Hello. Thank you for your hard work.

02:39.617 --> 02:41.578
You may leave now.

02:41.661 --> 02:42.620
Pardon?

02:42.704 --> 02:45.165
I'll come to the station
to file the report.

02:45.248 --> 02:48.960
I'm sorry,
but what's your relationship with her?

02:49.669 --> 02:50.753
We're family.

02:51.379 --> 02:52.338
[officer 1] Excuse me?

02:59.596 --> 03:00.805
She is…

03:02.307 --> 03:03.266
my wife.

03:04.684 --> 03:06.769
[slow music playing]

03:09.814 --> 03:10.815
[Sa-eon] Stay here.

03:13.192 --> 03:15.612
- My wife gave this case to me.
- He's Paik Sa-eon.

03:17.030 --> 03:17.906
[officer 2 stammers]

03:18.907 --> 03:20.533
I have a favor to ask.

03:21.367 --> 03:23.161
Yes, please go ahead.

03:23.244 --> 03:25.955
I'll visit as soon as I can
to file the report.

03:26.039 --> 03:30.376
In the meantime, please keep
our personal information private.

03:30.460 --> 03:32.337
Yes, of course.

03:32.420 --> 03:35.006
- We'll ensure strict security.
- [officer 1 chuckles softly]

03:35.965 --> 03:36.966
Thank you.

03:37.050 --> 03:38.051
By the way…

03:38.134 --> 03:41.512
- Don't do it. Don't.
- I also have a favor to ask.

03:41.596 --> 03:44.724
I know this isn't the greatest situation,

03:45.225 --> 03:47.352
but may I get a picture with you?

03:49.062 --> 03:50.605
If you keep your promise,

03:50.688 --> 03:53.191
I'll take a picture with you
at the station.

03:53.775 --> 03:55.026
I see. Okay.

03:55.610 --> 03:57.904
- Well, then.
- Okay, see you again.

03:58.613 --> 03:59.614
Go safely.

04:07.622 --> 04:08.665
[car starting]

04:17.924 --> 04:19.634
Your father's nurse…

04:20.718 --> 04:22.136
has my number.

04:23.304 --> 04:26.724
Anyway, we should move him
to a different nursing home.

04:29.227 --> 04:30.103
[sighs]

04:31.646 --> 04:33.022
How could he go so far?

04:36.401 --> 04:37.402
From now on,

04:39.153 --> 04:41.281
you don't have to worry about your father.

04:42.073 --> 04:43.324
I'll take care of it.

04:47.787 --> 04:48.663
[Hee-joo sobbing]

04:54.919 --> 04:56.921
[slow music playing]

05:01.592 --> 05:03.469
You're making sounds.

05:05.847 --> 05:07.181
[sniffles]

05:07.265 --> 05:08.224
[scoffs]

05:10.435 --> 05:11.394
Hong Hee-joo…

05:12.937 --> 05:14.272
can make sounds.

05:19.819 --> 05:21.571
[soft pop song playing]

05:22.363 --> 05:23.197
[sniffles]

05:23.281 --> 05:24.282
[scoffs]

05:26.701 --> 05:28.161
[softly] You look so ugly right now.

05:33.416 --> 05:34.375
[inhales deeply]

05:36.044 --> 05:37.837
I'm not telling you to stop crying.

05:40.548 --> 05:41.924
Cry as much as you want.

05:45.303 --> 05:46.554
[sniffles]

05:48.139 --> 05:49.640
[sobbing]

06:10.953 --> 06:14.290
One tteokbokki set with gimbap,
fish cakes, and sundae with the entrails.

06:14.373 --> 06:15.625
[exclaims] Can I have one?

06:15.708 --> 06:17.210
- Ow!
- Come more often!

06:17.293 --> 06:18.586
- Okay?
- [You-ri] I'm here!

06:18.669 --> 06:21.005
I'm just happy to see you.

06:21.089 --> 06:22.423
[You-ri exclaims]

06:22.507 --> 06:24.175
You get prettier by the day.

06:24.258 --> 06:25.468
I was always pretty.

06:26.677 --> 06:29.555
- [Sang-woo] Are you just getting off work?
- [You-ri] My goodness.

06:29.639 --> 06:30.515
[chuckles softly]

06:31.224 --> 06:33.726
We don't have a show today.
What brings you here?

06:34.310 --> 06:35.561
Well…

06:35.645 --> 06:37.105
[You-ri] Oh my.

06:37.772 --> 06:38.898
Don't tell me…

06:39.982 --> 06:41.818
Did you come hoping to run into me?

06:41.901 --> 06:42.902
[quirky music playing]

06:42.985 --> 06:43.945
[You-ri] Come on.

06:44.028 --> 06:47.824
We're visiting a site together
in a few days! [giggles]

06:47.907 --> 06:49.075
[Sang-woo chuckles nervously]

06:51.994 --> 06:52.995
[slurping]

06:55.206 --> 06:56.874
- I was kidding.
- [music fades]

06:58.793 --> 07:00.044
Do you live in Yeouido?

07:00.878 --> 07:03.422
- Yeah, it's near the hospital.
- [You-ri] Mmm.

07:04.215 --> 07:05.633
[gasps] Thank you.

07:05.716 --> 07:07.218
[snickering]

07:08.344 --> 07:09.804
[Sang-woo clears throat] Is it…

07:11.264 --> 07:12.306
your birthday today?

07:12.390 --> 07:14.600
- What?
- That looks like a feast.

07:15.435 --> 07:18.104
This is one serving for me.

07:18.187 --> 07:19.439
[Sang-woo] I see.

07:20.606 --> 07:24.986
That day at the French restaurant,
it didn't even make a dent in my stomach.

07:25.862 --> 07:26.737
Eat up.

07:29.115 --> 07:30.158
[You-ri giggles]

07:30.241 --> 07:31.659
[quirky music playing]

07:36.539 --> 07:37.373
Hey.

07:39.667 --> 07:41.085
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo.

07:42.128 --> 07:43.087
It's her, isn't it?

07:43.838 --> 07:45.047
Your secret crush.

07:46.674 --> 07:47.800
[You-ri chuckles]

07:48.426 --> 07:49.552
[Sang-woo exhales heavily]

07:52.138 --> 07:53.848
[You-ri] I could just tell that day.

07:53.931 --> 07:57.351
You said you've been through
unrequited love like a fan before.

07:57.435 --> 07:58.352
Remember?

07:58.436 --> 07:59.687
[Sang-woo clears throat]

07:59.770 --> 08:02.440
[Sang-woo] Well…
I'm curious about something too.

08:02.523 --> 08:03.733
Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon.

08:04.400 --> 08:06.569
Why are you such a big fan of him?

08:08.404 --> 08:09.489
[You-ri] Well…

08:10.531 --> 08:11.365
Me?

08:13.576 --> 08:15.411
I didn't like him at first.

08:16.662 --> 08:19.373
Actually, I was so scared of him.

08:19.457 --> 08:20.458
ON AIR

08:20.541 --> 08:24.504
[Sa-eon] Are you saying there are
no standards to regulate microplastics?

08:24.587 --> 08:29.050
Yes, a bill must be prepared
through National Assembly discussions.

08:29.759 --> 08:31.969
That's all that I've prepared.

08:32.053 --> 08:36.390
Then, what could be
realistic regulatory measures?

08:37.475 --> 08:38.434
Excuse me?

08:39.810 --> 08:41.145
MICROPLASTIC SWALLOWING THE OCEAN

08:41.229 --> 08:42.063
Well…

08:42.146 --> 08:43.147
[quirky music playing]

08:43.231 --> 08:47.985
First, we should reduce plastic use
and use tumblers instead of disposables.

08:48.069 --> 08:51.531
That would be more of an individual effort
and a recommendation.

08:52.240 --> 08:55.076
What could be legally prohibited?

08:55.159 --> 08:55.993
[You-ri] Well…

08:57.745 --> 08:59.372
Well…

09:01.332 --> 09:02.416
[Sa-eon] Anchor Na You-ri?

09:03.042 --> 09:04.919
Aside from just raising the issue,

09:05.002 --> 09:07.880
are there no concrete solutions prepared?

09:10.967 --> 09:14.011
[You-ri] Well… I…

09:15.304 --> 09:17.598
He's breaking in
a new recruit again. [chuckles]

09:17.682 --> 09:19.475
She looks like she'll cry.

09:22.687 --> 09:24.480
Thank you for your presentation.

09:30.361 --> 09:31.362
[music ends]

09:32.530 --> 09:33.406
[exhales heavily]

09:40.830 --> 09:42.415
Come in by two o'clock from tomorrow.

09:42.498 --> 09:43.416
[You-ri gasps]

09:44.125 --> 09:46.002
You mean, two o'clock in the morning?

09:47.837 --> 09:52.133
If you're to run it by me for review,
learn how to write it, and practice,

09:52.717 --> 09:53.843
it's not that early.

09:54.427 --> 09:57.972
You'll teach me yourself?

10:00.141 --> 10:03.561
An anchor isn't a parrot
that simply reads off a script.

10:04.228 --> 10:08.983
Plus, for the morning news, you should
come in by two to remove facial swelling.

10:09.066 --> 10:10.276
[Sa-eon scoffs]

10:10.359 --> 10:13.487
Look at your face now.
You look like a soggy steamed bun.

10:15.072 --> 10:16.490
[mellow music playing]

10:20.786 --> 10:21.662
[chuckles softly]

10:22.204 --> 10:23.831
He was scary,

10:24.707 --> 10:27.418
but he was a good colleague
who taught me a lot.

10:30.796 --> 10:31.964
But then one day,

10:32.048 --> 10:34.800
he quit his job
and got appointed as spokesperson.

10:34.884 --> 10:36.093
He even got married.

10:36.177 --> 10:39.513
- Now it's hard to see him once a year.
- Who did he marry?

10:47.104 --> 10:47.980
[sniffles]

10:49.565 --> 10:51.359
[amusing music playing]

10:54.320 --> 10:57.948
[softly] Sa-eon's family
is a famous political family.

10:58.032 --> 11:01.577
His grandfather's a bigwig who's done
everything except for the presidency.

11:01.661 --> 11:03.454
His father's
a strong presidential candidate.

11:03.537 --> 11:05.748
His relatives are
former or current ministers,

11:05.831 --> 11:07.500
prosecutor generals, mayors, lawmakers…

11:07.583 --> 11:10.586
Naturally, he married the daughter
of a very influential family.

11:11.837 --> 11:15.424
The eldest daughter of Chairman Hong
of Chungwoon Daily News.

11:23.057 --> 11:24.183
[Sa-eon sighs]

11:29.772 --> 11:32.733
Did you just remember
what day it is today?

11:40.074 --> 11:41.367
[Hee-joo] Why a hotel room?

11:41.450 --> 11:43.452
Wash your face. And blow your nose too.

11:50.626 --> 11:51.919
[line ringing]

11:53.212 --> 11:54.839
[man] Yes, this is room service.

12:02.555 --> 12:03.514
[sighs softly]

12:05.141 --> 12:06.225
[blows nose]

12:06.308 --> 12:08.436
[water running]

12:11.397 --> 12:12.273
[sighs]

12:15.151 --> 12:16.694
[Hee-joo] I need to get it together.

12:17.278 --> 12:19.864
I have to stay focused from now on.

12:30.958 --> 12:32.293
Should we talk now?

12:33.252 --> 12:34.086
Sit down.

12:37.882 --> 12:38.966
Take out your phone.

12:40.176 --> 12:41.343
Because from now on,

12:42.344 --> 12:43.804
I want us to have a conversation.

12:45.723 --> 12:48.100
- [Hee-joo] Not an interrogation?
- It's not an interrogation.

12:50.186 --> 12:51.270
As you know,

12:52.605 --> 12:55.065
someone's been messing with us lately.

12:56.025 --> 12:58.110
Your car, my office,

12:58.194 --> 13:00.654
and even your father's nursing home
this time.

13:01.155 --> 13:03.324
I haven't requested
a police investigation yet.

13:04.325 --> 13:05.534
But if this continues,

13:06.368 --> 13:07.703
I'll have no other choice.

13:10.831 --> 13:12.208
[slow, tense music playing]

13:12.291 --> 13:16.545
If you're the victim instead of me,
the police will start digging into you.

13:16.629 --> 13:21.133
So before that happens,
tell me if you're hiding anything.

13:27.890 --> 13:29.391
I guess there is something.

13:31.310 --> 13:32.353
[scoffs]

13:35.481 --> 13:39.610
I could keep pressuring you
until I force it out of you, but…

13:41.487 --> 13:42.321
I won't.

13:43.739 --> 13:45.324
I won't do that, Hee-joo.

13:46.700 --> 13:48.452
We're not close enough to interfere

13:49.578 --> 13:51.372
with each other's lives, right?

13:52.581 --> 13:53.457
[knock on door]

13:57.294 --> 13:58.379
Leave it at the door.

14:05.761 --> 14:07.972
[soft music playing]

14:15.229 --> 14:18.816
Eat this and rest.
Come down afterward. I'll go first.

14:29.743 --> 14:31.412
You haven't settled from the shock yet.

14:31.996 --> 14:35.541
You know you'll be very tense down there.

14:38.252 --> 14:40.754
Don't overdo it. Just do as I say.

14:51.015 --> 14:52.141
[door closes]

14:52.224 --> 14:54.226
[solemn music playing]

15:16.040 --> 15:17.249
[music ends]

15:24.965 --> 15:25.799
[gulps]

15:26.800 --> 15:27.635
Another glass.

15:29.345 --> 15:30.471
[drink pouring]

15:40.105 --> 15:41.982
- [door closes]
- Relax.

15:43.609 --> 15:44.443
What?

15:45.152 --> 15:46.153
[Ui-yong clears throat]

15:46.236 --> 15:47.655
[foot tapping]

15:49.406 --> 15:50.616
Ouch.

15:52.868 --> 15:54.370
Do you have a plan?

15:55.996 --> 15:57.373
[Ui-yong clears throat]

16:00.125 --> 16:03.170
It shouldn't just be
another regular meal today, right?

16:04.421 --> 16:06.215
Didn't the aides make a plan?

16:06.298 --> 16:08.300
I don't need a grand plan for this.

16:09.301 --> 16:11.053
A disobedient child?

16:11.136 --> 16:12.805
Just beat him until he obeys.

16:14.723 --> 16:15.724
Don't worry.

16:18.435 --> 16:19.645
[Ui-yong sighs]

16:21.230 --> 16:22.356
[elevator dings]

16:34.576 --> 16:36.578
[suspenseful music playing]

16:38.789 --> 16:39.748
[Ui-yong clears throat]

16:40.249 --> 16:41.250
[Kyu-jin] You're here.

16:44.753 --> 16:45.713
Why are you alone?

16:46.505 --> 16:47.339
Where is she?

16:49.717 --> 16:50.926
She's not feeling well.

16:51.010 --> 16:51.927
Call her.

16:56.265 --> 16:57.182
Did you not hear me?

16:57.891 --> 16:59.518
Bring her here right now.

16:59.601 --> 17:00.978
Let's eat.

17:01.854 --> 17:03.856
I only have an hour to spare.

17:05.024 --> 17:07.651
Didn't you have something to say to me?

17:12.990 --> 17:14.992
[suspenseful music continues]

17:32.801 --> 17:33.635
[gasps]

17:40.059 --> 17:41.810
Appear on a show?

17:41.894 --> 17:42.728
[Ui-yong] Yeah.

17:43.562 --> 17:46.857
A special on presidential candidates.
Just anyone does it these days.

17:47.441 --> 17:50.611
You know, cooking, dancing, and singing.

17:51.320 --> 17:52.154
[scoffs]

17:54.114 --> 17:55.324
Come when we're filming.

17:59.036 --> 18:00.037
[knock on door]

18:03.415 --> 18:04.416
[music ends]

18:04.500 --> 18:05.876
Come and sit.

18:14.093 --> 18:15.094
[sighs]

18:15.803 --> 18:18.597
Others bring their sons, daughters-in-law,

18:18.680 --> 18:22.434
and even their dogs and cats
to promote themselves.

18:23.685 --> 18:25.395
But our family… [chuckles]

18:25.479 --> 18:28.148
The only thing I can boast about
is my son.

18:29.775 --> 18:32.611
Have you still not heard from your sister?

18:32.694 --> 18:34.154
Don't bring that up again.

18:34.238 --> 18:37.324
You know, I really think
Chairman Hong tricked me.

18:37.407 --> 18:40.828
He never intended to give us
his eldest daughter in the first place.

18:40.911 --> 18:43.163
Right? He's so skeptical.

18:43.914 --> 18:45.833
He's scared I might lose the election.

18:45.916 --> 18:48.752
That's why he sent his flawed daughter
as a stand-in.

18:48.836 --> 18:50.879
[slow music playing]

18:50.963 --> 18:52.506
What exactly is your purpose?

18:53.257 --> 18:56.385
Even if you were a bargain,
you should be able to earn your keep.

18:56.969 --> 18:58.971
Why can't you do anything?

19:04.268 --> 19:05.435
[Kyu-jin] What are you doing?

19:06.103 --> 19:07.646
It's rude. We're eating.

19:07.729 --> 19:08.564
[music fades]

19:08.647 --> 19:09.606
[Sa-eon] Bring it.

19:14.194 --> 19:16.196
[mysterious music playing]

19:18.824 --> 19:20.075
[camera shutter clicks]

19:23.662 --> 19:24.955
Welcome.

19:26.790 --> 19:29.418
There's a paparazzi
taking pictures of guests here.

19:33.755 --> 19:37.009
"Spokesperson Paik Sa-eon meets with
his father, Paik Ui-yong, for dinner."

19:37.968 --> 19:39.887
"Will he join the election campaign?"

19:40.929 --> 19:42.431
Is that the headline you wanted?

19:44.683 --> 19:47.603
I'll decide whether or not to participate
in your election.

19:47.686 --> 19:50.105
Coercion, threats, subtle manipulation.

19:50.189 --> 19:51.523
Don't even think of it.

19:54.151 --> 19:55.652
[Ui-yong] You little punk.

19:58.071 --> 19:58.906
[music fades]

20:06.788 --> 20:08.790
[solemn music playing]

20:11.919 --> 20:13.295
You arrogant brat.

20:16.590 --> 20:17.507
You punk.

20:17.591 --> 20:20.385
Do you know what will happen
if you keep acting like this?

20:21.053 --> 20:24.932
The moment you step out of my shadow,
you could get crushed completely.

20:26.099 --> 20:28.977
Do you really think I'm still in there?

20:29.061 --> 20:30.145
What did you say?

20:33.190 --> 20:34.024
Wait.

20:35.609 --> 20:36.693
It's not you, is it?

20:36.777 --> 20:37.694
What do you mean?

20:38.528 --> 20:41.073
I know you'd do anything
to get me to surrender.

20:42.157 --> 20:44.826
- So the thought crossed my mind.
- What are you talking about?

20:44.910 --> 20:46.161
Make some damn sense!

20:50.415 --> 20:51.875
I'll say one thing.

20:53.001 --> 20:55.671
You're at the threshold
of being president, thanks to Grandfather.

20:55.754 --> 20:59.132
The least you could do
is step over it on your own.

20:59.216 --> 21:00.759
Don't whine

21:01.718 --> 21:03.011
and ask me to push you.

21:04.388 --> 21:05.222
What?

21:08.976 --> 21:10.852
- Are you done?
- I am.

21:13.563 --> 21:14.898
And I'll leave now.

21:18.277 --> 21:19.695
[footsteps receding]

21:21.405 --> 21:23.907
[Kyu-jin sighs] Was this your plan?

21:24.992 --> 21:26.243
You ruined everything.

21:26.952 --> 21:28.078
[breath trembling]

21:28.161 --> 21:30.706
That punk started it!

21:32.165 --> 21:33.208
Damn it.

21:34.209 --> 21:35.460
That damned punk.

21:37.170 --> 21:38.338
[sighs in exasperation]

21:41.758 --> 21:43.176
[slow music playing]

21:48.557 --> 21:49.558
I bet you…

21:50.475 --> 21:51.893
want to divorce me.

21:54.062 --> 21:56.815
You married me in place
of your missing sister and can't speak.

21:57.399 --> 22:00.110
So you can't even defend yourself
when your in-laws spout nonsense.

22:00.193 --> 22:01.486
[Sa-eon's breath trembling]

22:06.408 --> 22:08.994
They're people
who can easily replace their children.

22:09.661 --> 22:10.912
So whatever they say,

22:11.872 --> 22:14.875
don't listen to them or take it to heart.

22:17.252 --> 22:18.086
[music ends]

22:20.881 --> 22:22.090
[phone vibrating]

22:23.258 --> 22:26.386
PARK DO-JAE

22:28.472 --> 22:29.306
Go inside.

22:30.766 --> 22:31.850
[phone vibrating]

22:34.811 --> 22:35.812
[car door closes]

22:38.065 --> 22:39.191
Yes, go ahead.

22:40.901 --> 22:43.945
The detective in charge
of the nursing home incident just called.

22:44.029 --> 22:47.324
He said the blood analysis results
confirmed animal blood and fake teeth.

22:47.407 --> 22:48.575
Animal?

22:50.619 --> 22:51.620
[scoffs]

22:53.371 --> 22:55.123
Okay.

22:55.207 --> 22:58.585
Also, I have a personal request.

23:02.506 --> 23:04.341
[breathing heavily]

23:04.925 --> 23:06.635
[mysterious music playing]

23:08.178 --> 23:10.263
[Jin-cheol whispering] Call…

23:10.347 --> 23:12.724
Call him.

23:14.101 --> 23:16.770
Sis.

23:18.146 --> 23:21.733
- [static over radio]
- [kidnapper] No backing out in the middle.

23:22.609 --> 23:24.402
You started this,

23:25.529 --> 23:26.905
so you see it through.

23:26.988 --> 23:28.281
Got it?

23:28.365 --> 23:32.494
Sis! [laughing maniacally]

23:34.955 --> 23:35.789
[Hee-joo] I can't…

23:36.790 --> 23:38.333
do this anymore.

23:39.793 --> 23:41.795
[dramatic music playing]

23:47.175 --> 23:48.343
[breathing heavily]

23:56.184 --> 23:57.227
Where are you going?

23:58.687 --> 23:59.896
[music fades]

24:00.522 --> 24:01.356
Is that trash?

24:02.607 --> 24:03.441
Give it to me.

24:06.444 --> 24:07.529
I'll take it out.

24:18.081 --> 24:19.457
[phone ringing]

24:24.254 --> 24:26.423
DIRECTOR HAN JIN-E

24:28.008 --> 24:29.551
- [Jin-e] Hey, Hee-joo!
- [man] Hee-joo!

24:30.635 --> 24:32.888
You can do this! Good luck! You got this!

24:32.971 --> 24:33.889
[all] Good luck!

24:33.972 --> 24:34.848
[Jin-e] Let's go!

24:34.931 --> 24:37.601
- [all] To the president's office!
- [all cheering]

24:38.268 --> 24:39.769
[Hee-joo] Thanks, everyone.

24:39.853 --> 24:41.104
Don't mention it.

24:41.771 --> 24:43.106
Dinner's on you if you pass!

24:43.190 --> 24:44.774
Good luck! We love you!

24:47.152 --> 24:48.570
[Sa-eon] I'll wish you luck too.

24:48.653 --> 24:49.946
You'll pass.

24:58.330 --> 24:59.998
[Hee-joo] If I get it, what then?

25:00.081 --> 25:02.125
[slow music playing]

25:02.209 --> 25:03.543
What do you mean?

25:05.378 --> 25:06.880
We talked about this before.

25:06.963 --> 25:09.841
If our families find out
I'm working beside you…

25:09.925 --> 25:11.301
Hong Hee-joo. [sighs]

25:12.427 --> 25:15.055
How much longer
will you live as the obedient child?

25:15.889 --> 25:17.849
Aren't you sick of others
telling you what to do?

25:18.683 --> 25:20.894
It's your chance to try
with your name on the line.

25:21.811 --> 25:24.856
Chicken out and blow it
or give up over what others think.

25:25.899 --> 25:26.816
Do whatever you want.

25:36.910 --> 25:38.078
[Hee-joo] Okay.

25:38.161 --> 25:39.663
Then you should start thinking about

25:39.746 --> 25:42.332
how you're going to handle
the aftermath if I get the job.

25:47.712 --> 25:48.630
[door opens]

25:50.298 --> 25:51.299
[door closes]

25:52.425 --> 25:53.426
[Sa-eon scoffs]

25:54.427 --> 25:55.428
[music fades]

25:57.138 --> 25:58.139
[sighs softly]

25:59.349 --> 26:00.392
[phone vibrates]

26:04.437 --> 26:05.855
PARK DO-JAE

26:07.607 --> 26:10.402
[Do-jae] I looked into what you asked for.

26:12.153 --> 26:15.031
WE MEET ANOTHER FAMILY MEMBER TODAY

26:21.121 --> 26:22.831
[Sa-eon] Looks good. Let's go with this.

26:31.631 --> 26:32.757
[sighs]

26:39.556 --> 26:42.434
Our spokesperson has never been this late
to work before.

26:42.517 --> 26:43.977
Is something wrong?

26:44.060 --> 26:46.563
[Do-jae] He has matters to take care of,
so he'll be late.

26:47.647 --> 26:49.232
[keyboard clacking]

26:52.944 --> 26:54.946
- Hello.
- Hello.

26:56.614 --> 26:58.241
[playful music playing]

27:03.204 --> 27:05.415
- I have something to report.
- Me too.

27:06.082 --> 27:07.625
It's urgent. I'll go first.

27:07.709 --> 27:08.710
Mine's urgent too.

27:09.919 --> 27:11.129
[Sa-eon] Mr. Park.

27:11.212 --> 27:12.047
Yes, sir.

27:23.600 --> 27:25.143
[music ends]

27:25.226 --> 27:26.353
I'm the section chief.

27:28.271 --> 27:31.441
I have something to discuss
regarding the voice modulation.

27:31.524 --> 27:32.692
Did you find something?

27:32.776 --> 27:35.070
If we analyze
the waveform and spectrogram,

27:35.153 --> 27:38.907
I think we'll be able to determine
the pitch range, age, and gender.

27:38.990 --> 27:40.283
We don't need the gender.

27:40.867 --> 27:43.453
To be honest, I'm not curious
about that pervert's voice.

27:44.120 --> 27:46.581
Just in case, it might be someone I know.

27:46.664 --> 27:48.583
- That's why I want to unmask him.
- Okay.

27:48.666 --> 27:50.460
I'll report it as soon as it's done.

27:50.960 --> 27:51.795
Okay.

27:51.878 --> 27:54.297
And this is regarding Ji Sang-woo.

27:56.674 --> 27:57.926
A lot of his videos

27:58.009 --> 28:00.804
are about unsolved cases
related to arson and bombs.

28:00.887 --> 28:04.349
He seems to be very knowledgeable
about explosions and arson methods.

28:05.058 --> 28:07.727
And currently,
he's appearing on HBC's Crime Report.

28:07.811 --> 28:09.979
It's a mystery crime program.

28:11.231 --> 28:12.399
"Crime Report"?

28:15.610 --> 28:16.444
[exhales]

28:16.528 --> 28:17.654
Okay.

28:17.737 --> 28:19.155
- You're excused.
- Yes, sir.

28:28.915 --> 28:29.999
[Young-woo] Sir.

28:30.917 --> 28:33.670
It's the final interview list
for the sign language interpreters.

28:35.588 --> 28:36.589
HONG HEE-JOO

28:37.173 --> 28:39.634
The interviews will start soon.
Will you join?

28:45.348 --> 28:47.392
[mellow music playing]

28:47.475 --> 28:48.727
CANDIDATE ID
HONG HEE-JOO

28:49.853 --> 28:52.480
[Sa-eon] It's your chance to try
with your name on the line.

28:52.564 --> 28:55.442
Chicken out and blow it
or give up over what others think.

28:56.568 --> 28:57.652
Do whatever you want.

29:00.447 --> 29:01.281
[door opens]

29:05.201 --> 29:08.788
Candidate 24, 25, and 26, please be ready.

29:14.919 --> 29:18.006
2024 PRESIDENTIAL OFFICE
SIGN LANGUAGE INTERPRETER INTERVIEW

29:19.007 --> 29:21.760
You'll conduct a real briefing
for the final interview.

29:21.843 --> 29:23.261
It'll be a practical exam.

29:23.344 --> 29:25.096
In case of real-time interpretation,

29:25.180 --> 29:28.725
quick thinking and sign language speed
are especially important.

29:28.808 --> 29:31.019
I'll play an existing briefing video.

29:31.102 --> 29:32.103
Candidate…

29:32.812 --> 29:35.648
number 24, Hong Hee-joo,
we'll start with you.

29:43.114 --> 29:44.199
PRESIDENTIAL OFFICE

29:44.282 --> 29:46.034
[mellow music playing]

29:49.245 --> 29:52.040
[Hee-joo] The 2020
Korea-Egypt summit briefing.

29:52.123 --> 29:55.710
[Sa-eon] Korea and Egypt
have complementary industrial structures,

29:55.794 --> 29:59.047
which offer great potential
for expanding trade and investment.

29:59.130 --> 29:59.964
It is hoped that

30:00.048 --> 30:03.134
the Korea-Egypt Trade and Economic
Partnership Joint Research MOU

30:03.218 --> 30:05.512
will lead to an FTA
between the two countries.

30:05.595 --> 30:08.807
Also, it was expressed that
there's hope for cooperative projects

30:08.890 --> 30:11.017
to strengthen administrative capabilities

30:11.100 --> 30:13.895
by sharing South Korea's
digital information expertise.

30:13.978 --> 30:16.815
Furthermore, both countries agreed
to open a new chapter

30:16.898 --> 30:20.568
of mutually beneficial cooperation
in key areas such as economic investment,

30:20.652 --> 30:23.112
cultural heritage preservation
and management,

30:23.196 --> 30:26.282
energy, advanced technologies,
and defense,

30:26.366 --> 30:29.118
aiming to establish
a comprehensive partnership

30:29.202 --> 30:31.037
between the two nations.

30:31.120 --> 30:34.624
As emphasized, this will boost
our country's overall competitiveness.

30:35.208 --> 30:36.209
[candidate] Thank you.

30:37.252 --> 30:38.211
[phone vibrating]

30:38.294 --> 30:40.046
[intriguing music playing]

30:40.129 --> 30:41.005
Excuse me.

30:43.424 --> 30:44.259
Yes?

30:46.427 --> 30:47.554
I understand.

30:51.850 --> 30:53.434
SPOKESPERSON BRIEFING

31:00.400 --> 31:02.402
[captivating music playing]

31:14.998 --> 31:15.832
[door opens]

31:24.215 --> 31:25.592
[music fades]

31:25.675 --> 31:28.428
Candidate number 24,
interpreter Hong Hee-joo.

31:28.511 --> 31:32.140
I want you to answer
the questions I ask honestly.

31:34.100 --> 31:36.269
Did you know the script in advance?

31:36.352 --> 31:38.479
It wasn't simultaneous interpretation.

31:38.563 --> 31:41.983
I noticed that you signed
before I even spoke sometimes.

31:42.734 --> 31:44.068
How will you explain this?

31:46.112 --> 31:47.864
I practiced to these videos.

31:49.991 --> 31:50.992
If that's the case,

31:52.118 --> 31:54.787
can we test you with a different video?

31:55.496 --> 31:56.331
[interviewer] Yes.

31:58.958 --> 32:00.418
[intriguing music playing]

32:08.635 --> 32:10.303
[Sa-eon on TV] For a healthy society,

32:10.386 --> 32:15.600
all citizens must unite
in caring for and educating children.

32:15.683 --> 32:19.812
This is something that all members
of society must participate in.

32:19.896 --> 32:20.772
Enough.

32:20.855 --> 32:22.023
Next video.

32:22.649 --> 32:25.652
[Sa-eon on TV] Our government
has consistently expressed its willingness

32:25.735 --> 32:27.862
to engage in dialogue
to resolve the issue.

32:27.946 --> 32:29.948
- [Sa-eon] Next.
- Diplomatic communication…

32:30.031 --> 32:31.240
In the current situation

32:31.324 --> 32:33.701
where business leaders
are facing difficulties

32:33.785 --> 32:37.372
and everyone is trying their best
in their respective positions,

32:37.455 --> 32:39.499
- we must answer what truly…
- [Sa-eon] Next.

32:39.582 --> 32:40.708
…serves the people…

32:40.792 --> 32:43.920
To prevent further harm
to the victim's reputation

32:44.003 --> 32:47.882
through reports where even the facts
have not been verified,

32:47.966 --> 32:50.969
- I ask that journalists exercise caution.
- [in English] Stop.

32:51.052 --> 32:52.512
[music fades]

32:52.595 --> 32:54.722
[in Korean] Did you practice
to all of these?

32:56.683 --> 32:57.517
Yes.

32:59.143 --> 33:02.647
It'll be the same
with any other video you play.

33:03.898 --> 33:06.067
Why have you memorized all the videos?

33:06.859 --> 33:10.989
[interviewer] I practiced a lot
with your videos.

33:11.614 --> 33:14.909
They were chosen at random,
regardless of the year or content.

33:14.993 --> 33:18.371
But your hands move at the same speed
and timing as my voice.

33:18.997 --> 33:21.416
Is that a coincidence?
It's not just once or twice.

33:22.834 --> 33:25.294
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo,
answer my question.

33:37.890 --> 33:40.727
What did you just say?

33:42.812 --> 33:44.230
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo!

33:49.485 --> 33:52.321
I said I did it because I was crazy.

33:52.405 --> 33:53.531
[snorts] Wow.

33:53.614 --> 33:54.532
She was crazy.

33:56.034 --> 33:57.452
[slow music playing]

33:58.369 --> 34:01.706
[interviewer] I was obsessed
with your briefings, Mr. Paik.

34:02.290 --> 34:04.959
[Hee-joo] I've dreamed of becoming
a sign language interpreter

34:05.084 --> 34:06.461
for a government agency.

34:06.544 --> 34:08.129
That became excessive…

34:08.212 --> 34:10.465
This is the result of intense practicing?

34:10.548 --> 34:13.468
[Hee-joo] How your upper lip
and upper teeth move

34:13.551 --> 34:17.597
when you set your articulation points,
I studied that a lot in particular.

34:17.680 --> 34:18.931
I can predict consonants

34:19.015 --> 34:22.101
from the sounds your tongue makes
against the roof of your mouth.

34:22.185 --> 34:24.479
So, as soon as I open my mouth…

34:24.562 --> 34:25.396
No, wait.

34:26.189 --> 34:29.025
Your hands move faster
when you predict it?

34:29.609 --> 34:32.195
And you studied it that obsessively?

34:32.278 --> 34:36.783
[Hee-joo] I mimicked,
practiced, and dug into it.

34:36.866 --> 34:38.367
[slow music continues playing]

34:40.036 --> 34:41.037
[flips page]

34:42.830 --> 34:43.873
[Sa-eon] But…

34:43.956 --> 34:46.084
can you not speak at all?

34:47.585 --> 34:48.503
[music ends]

34:50.296 --> 34:52.799
Personal disabilities
aren't disqualifying factors,

34:52.882 --> 34:54.634
so she passed the document review.

34:55.343 --> 34:59.889
And the job of an interpreter is to listen
and convey it with their hands, so…

35:00.389 --> 35:01.808
If you get the job,

35:01.891 --> 35:05.478
how will you communicate
with the spokesperson's team?

35:15.446 --> 35:16.322
[phone vibrates]

35:16.405 --> 35:19.367
2024 PRESIDENTIAL OFFICE
SIGN LANGUAGE INTERPRETER INTERVIEW

35:21.661 --> 35:23.579
[Young-woo] I don't know why,
but he's fixated.

35:24.163 --> 35:25.289
It might take a while.

35:27.083 --> 35:28.960
[Do-jae] The interview is running behind.

35:29.043 --> 35:30.670
I hope you understand.

35:38.386 --> 35:41.222
[interviewer] Can you use sign language?

35:41.305 --> 35:43.766
[Hee-joo] If you can't, I'll teach you.

35:43.850 --> 35:45.768
You need to learn so you can see

35:45.852 --> 35:48.813
whether we interpreters are conveying
your message properly.

35:49.397 --> 35:52.358
If the nuance is off,
you can correct it right away.

35:52.441 --> 35:54.277
Sign language isn't difficult.

35:54.902 --> 35:58.698
If you learn it, there won't be issues
communicating with me either.

35:58.781 --> 36:01.200
You're right. That's a good idea.

36:05.496 --> 36:07.582
We'll discuss that if you get the job.

36:08.457 --> 36:09.375
Finally,

36:10.042 --> 36:11.669
I want to test you on something.

36:12.336 --> 36:14.797
I'll read a document
that you've never seen before,

36:14.881 --> 36:16.382
on the spot.

36:17.300 --> 36:18.801
Can you do it?

36:20.219 --> 36:22.013
- [interviewer] Yes.
- [Sa-eon inhales deeply]

36:22.096 --> 36:23.931
Then, let's begin.

36:27.643 --> 36:29.228
[slow music playing]

36:29.312 --> 36:30.146
Couple's Day…

36:31.772 --> 36:34.192
is a national observance
established to remind us

36:35.151 --> 36:38.070
of the importance of marital relationships

36:38.154 --> 36:40.489
and to encourage
the building of harmonious families.

36:41.199 --> 36:43.618
There's a couple here now.

36:44.994 --> 36:46.537
[tense music playing]

36:46.621 --> 36:50.291
The two have lived
without being able to open up

36:51.167 --> 36:52.418
to each other.

36:56.547 --> 36:58.216
Would things have been different…

37:00.718 --> 37:02.803
if they had been more honest

37:04.222 --> 37:05.598
and shown their true feelings?

37:08.392 --> 37:10.102
If they try to make an effort now,

37:11.979 --> 37:14.607
could they live
like any other ordinary couple?

37:17.485 --> 37:18.903
Yet again today,

37:20.029 --> 37:21.280
like how a mind game is played,

37:22.365 --> 37:24.533
the couple merely tries to read
each other's minds.

37:25.326 --> 37:26.827
The ironic thing is that

37:28.412 --> 37:31.832
their behavior is surprisingly similar.

37:31.916 --> 37:33.125
[music ends]

37:40.716 --> 37:42.843
[dramatic music playing]

37:54.188 --> 37:55.022
That's enough.

37:55.898 --> 37:57.191
Let's stop here.

38:03.364 --> 38:04.282
[door slams]

38:14.959 --> 38:15.960
[exhales sharply]

38:18.421 --> 38:21.716
[Hee-joo] I can assure you,
there's no one better than me.

38:22.466 --> 38:24.343
I can tell by a person's expression.

38:24.427 --> 38:27.388
I know what you're going to say
and what you're thinking.

38:29.557 --> 38:33.352
I mimicked, practiced, and dug into it.

38:33.936 --> 38:34.770
[scoffs]

38:36.105 --> 38:37.106
Hong Hee-joo.

38:39.817 --> 38:40.901
What are you…

38:42.528 --> 38:43.446
[sighs wearily]

38:52.705 --> 38:54.707
[slow music playing]

38:56.625 --> 38:58.961
CANDIDATE ID
HONG HEE-JOO

39:04.091 --> 39:05.718
[Hee-joo] I did a good job.

39:06.927 --> 39:07.928
Well done.

39:17.813 --> 39:19.815
[suspenseful music playing]

39:39.293 --> 39:40.127
[music ends]

39:40.711 --> 39:41.670
[phone vibrates]

39:47.093 --> 39:49.387
[Hee-joo] Classy County?

39:51.639 --> 39:53.557
We should move him
to a different nursing home.

39:57.144 --> 39:58.646
[celebrity 1 on TV] Tell me about it.

39:59.230 --> 40:01.148
[celebrity 2 on TV] He's an anchor.

40:01.232 --> 40:02.900
[celebrity 3 on TV] You weren't a farmer?

40:02.983 --> 40:06.195
That'll be hard in old age too.

40:06.278 --> 40:07.279
So true.

40:07.363 --> 40:08.364
[chuckles]

40:11.617 --> 40:12.451
[Hee-joo] Ta-da.

40:12.993 --> 40:14.995
Dried persimmons. Your favorite.

40:15.079 --> 40:17.081
Yeah, they're good.

40:17.748 --> 40:19.792
- [Hee-joo] They're from Sangju.
- [Jin-cheol] Yeah.

40:21.710 --> 40:23.921
Dad, do you like it here?

40:24.547 --> 40:25.381
Tastes good.

40:25.464 --> 40:26.465
[Hee-joo chuckles softly]

40:27.174 --> 40:29.844
[Hee-joo] It's much nicer
than before, right?

40:29.927 --> 40:30.928
[Jin-cheol] Mmm.

40:33.472 --> 40:34.306
Dad?

40:35.850 --> 40:37.017
I'm sorry.

40:37.977 --> 40:39.854
That will never happen again.

40:39.937 --> 40:40.938
Don't worry, okay?

40:42.940 --> 40:44.358
[Jin-cheol laughs]

41:01.667 --> 41:02.710
Dad, who did--

41:02.793 --> 41:04.128
"Don't worry, Father."

41:04.962 --> 41:09.175
"No matter what happens,
I'll protect you and Hee-joo."

41:10.676 --> 41:12.136
[mellow music playing]

41:15.014 --> 41:16.474
[Jin-cheol chuckles]

41:18.726 --> 41:20.227
He came here?

41:33.782 --> 41:34.742
[groans]

41:35.242 --> 41:36.285
Warm, right?

41:38.204 --> 41:39.205
[clicks tongue]

41:39.872 --> 41:42.583
So warm yet so cold.

41:43.751 --> 41:45.878
So harsh yet so kind.

41:48.506 --> 41:50.299
I can't figure him out.

41:51.634 --> 41:54.136
I thought I knew him well…

41:54.720 --> 41:57.097
- [Jin-cheol chuckles]
- …but I don't think I do at all.

42:05.564 --> 42:08.359
Today's sign language interpreter
interview evaluation.

42:09.151 --> 42:10.861
Is the press release ready?

42:10.945 --> 42:11.987
It's being finalized.

42:13.447 --> 42:14.323
By the way,

42:15.074 --> 42:18.327
about interpreter Hong Hee-joo
who had an interview earlier,

42:18.410 --> 42:22.331
were you pleased with her or not?

42:22.414 --> 42:24.208
Why do you want to know that?

42:24.291 --> 42:25.125
Excuse me?

42:26.001 --> 42:27.461
Because…

42:29.922 --> 42:35.010
Everyone found out
you turned the interview room upside down,

42:35.094 --> 42:37.346
so we made a bet for fun…

42:37.429 --> 42:38.556
[Sa-eon] A bet?

42:38.639 --> 42:39.807
For fun?

42:40.391 --> 42:42.893
We were about to, but we decided not to,
and we won't.

42:42.977 --> 42:45.145
What? A bet? No way.

42:45.229 --> 42:48.023
In this crucial decision
to select an interpreter

42:48.107 --> 42:50.025
to be the voice of our office…

42:56.532 --> 42:57.992
By the way, I like her.

42:59.910 --> 43:03.372
Interpreter Hong Hee-joo,
who studied you so passionately.

43:10.004 --> 43:10.838
So do I.

43:13.507 --> 43:14.341
I like her.

43:15.342 --> 43:16.468
Pardon?

43:21.599 --> 43:22.516
[door opens]

43:23.684 --> 43:24.602
[door closes]

43:32.359 --> 43:34.111
HONG HEE-JOO

43:34.194 --> 43:36.196
[mellow music playing]

43:38.240 --> 43:39.783
- [bottle pops]
- [exclaims]

43:41.160 --> 43:43.078
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

43:43.162 --> 43:44.079
[both chuckling]

43:47.082 --> 43:49.084
[indistinct chatter]

44:03.724 --> 44:04.600
[exhales]

44:05.559 --> 44:07.311
[mellow music continues playing]

44:22.076 --> 44:23.452
[Kyu-jin] You didn't eat anything.

44:23.535 --> 44:27.289
Not eating as an invited guest
is considered disrespectful.

44:28.999 --> 44:30.167
Eat it.

44:32.419 --> 44:33.545
My son…

44:35.422 --> 44:36.799
likes fish.

45:01.448 --> 45:03.158
[Yeon-hui] Stop stuffing your face!

45:03.700 --> 45:05.411
I didn't eat anything yet.

45:05.494 --> 45:06.328
[Yeon-hui sighs]

45:07.496 --> 45:09.206
I told you not to act pathetic.

45:09.289 --> 45:10.207
[utensil clatters]

45:12.167 --> 45:14.044
Learn from your sister.

45:18.590 --> 45:19.591
[music ends]

45:22.052 --> 45:24.054
[indistinct chatter]

45:31.603 --> 45:33.021
[young Sa-eon] Let's switch.

45:36.024 --> 45:36.900
Eat it.

45:39.111 --> 45:41.113
[soft pop song playing]

45:47.327 --> 45:49.079
[coughing]

45:52.875 --> 45:54.042
Slow down.

45:58.005 --> 45:59.089
What's your name?

46:05.053 --> 46:05.888
"Hong."

46:07.014 --> 46:07.848
"Hee."

46:09.975 --> 46:10.809
"Joo."

46:10.893 --> 46:11.727
HONG HEE-JOO

46:12.561 --> 46:13.395
"Hong Hee-joo"?

46:24.072 --> 46:25.657
When did you grow up so much?

46:27.034 --> 46:28.118
[phone vibrates]

46:35.542 --> 46:36.793
[Hee-joo] Thank you.

46:37.794 --> 46:39.963
You changed my dad's nursing home.

46:44.885 --> 46:46.386
He read it right away.

46:53.477 --> 46:54.728
[phone vibrates]

46:58.565 --> 47:00.901
HONG IN-A

47:01.985 --> 47:02.903
[song fades]

47:03.820 --> 47:06.031
[mysterious music playing]

47:18.794 --> 47:20.128
What are you saying?

47:20.212 --> 47:23.340
You want me to go in In-a's place
at the wedding tomorrow?

47:23.423 --> 47:25.425
Have you ever imagined that, Hee-joo?

47:25.509 --> 47:27.678
You and I come from humble beginnings,

47:27.761 --> 47:31.306
and now we'll be
the future president's in-laws! [laughs]

47:34.101 --> 47:35.602
- [door opens]
- [exclaims]

47:38.230 --> 47:40.232
[gripping music playing]

48:02.713 --> 48:03.630
[Sa-eon] Keep it safe.

48:08.552 --> 48:09.886
If the real owner returns,

48:10.596 --> 48:12.514
you might have to give it back.

48:12.598 --> 48:14.516
[gripping music continues playing]

48:35.203 --> 48:36.121
[music fades]

48:36.872 --> 48:37.748
[chuckles softly]

48:42.044 --> 48:43.253
[You-ri inhales sharply]

48:45.380 --> 48:46.381
Start.

48:48.884 --> 48:50.010
SA-EON

48:50.093 --> 48:51.303
- [phone vibrating]
- [gasps]

48:51.386 --> 48:53.764
What? Right now? At this hour?

48:53.847 --> 48:55.182
- [phone vibrating]
- Why?

48:55.724 --> 48:59.811
No, wait. Don't overthink it.
Just answer it. [clears throat]

48:59.895 --> 49:01.188
[chuckles softly]

49:04.066 --> 49:06.068
Hello? Sa-eon?

49:06.151 --> 49:08.320
[Sa-eon] Hey, it's me.
I only have three minutes.

49:08.403 --> 49:09.363
I'll make it quick.

49:09.446 --> 49:10.405
Oh my.

49:11.239 --> 49:14.242
By chance, did you just add water
to your cup noodles too?

49:14.326 --> 49:16.244
No, I'm driving.

49:16.328 --> 49:18.288
[You-ri] Oh, I see.

49:18.372 --> 49:19.998
Ji Sang-woo I met the other day.

49:20.082 --> 49:22.542
- He's doing a program with you, right?
- [You-ri] Yes.

49:23.168 --> 49:26.380
Age 34. Yeonhui University College
of Medicine, class of 2010.

49:26.463 --> 49:29.132
Director of Bliss Care Clinic.
Do you know anything else about him?

49:29.216 --> 49:30.676
[scoffs]

49:30.759 --> 49:33.053
Did you run a background check on him?

49:33.136 --> 49:36.056
Do you know anything about him
that's not on the website?

49:36.139 --> 49:37.516
I have two minutes left.

49:39.351 --> 49:41.353
Well…

49:42.062 --> 49:44.064
Right. He lives in Yeouido.

49:44.147 --> 49:45.190
Near the HBC building.

49:45.899 --> 49:47.234
- And.
- And?

49:47.859 --> 49:49.569
And…

49:49.653 --> 49:51.780
He grew up in an orphanage! [gasps]

49:51.863 --> 49:52.823
An orphanage?

49:52.906 --> 49:55.075
[You-ri] No! Never mind!

49:56.034 --> 49:57.744
[suspenseful music playing]

49:57.828 --> 49:59.121
NURI DREAM CENTER

50:00.455 --> 50:02.332
Is it Nuri Dream Center?

50:03.083 --> 50:05.168
Formerly known as Sinil Childcare Center?

50:05.752 --> 50:06.837
How did you know?

50:09.548 --> 50:10.424
But…

50:11.007 --> 50:12.634
why do you want to know?

50:12.718 --> 50:13.677
I'm out of time.

50:13.760 --> 50:15.721
- Enjoy your noodles.
- [line disconnects]

50:20.517 --> 50:22.018
[phone vibrating]

50:26.189 --> 50:27.983
It seems you messed up again, 406.

50:28.567 --> 50:30.318
[Hee-joo] You asked me before,

50:30.402 --> 50:34.197
what do I get in return
if you get rid of Hong Hee-joo?

50:34.865 --> 50:37.284
[in distorted voice]
I'll answer that question.

50:37.367 --> 50:38.744
[tense music playing]

50:38.827 --> 50:39.745
What is it?

50:41.371 --> 50:42.205
Hong In-a.

50:50.297 --> 50:52.591
In-a needs a place to return to.

50:53.216 --> 50:56.011
You and your family wanted

50:56.094 --> 50:58.472
Hong In-a from the start anyway.

50:58.555 --> 50:59.806
Hong Hee-joo…

51:02.184 --> 51:04.519
is just a stand-in puppet.

51:07.189 --> 51:08.023
There.

51:09.232 --> 51:11.276
So get rid of Hong Hee-joo.

51:12.027 --> 51:14.654
Before Hong In-a returns
and complicates things,

51:14.738 --> 51:15.947
take care of Hong Hee-joo--

51:16.031 --> 51:19.993
- [Sa-eon] 406, you don't know anything.
- What?

51:22.287 --> 51:24.498
I'll only say this once,
so listen carefully.

51:25.499 --> 51:27.542
Before Hong In-a disappeared,

51:27.626 --> 51:30.754
the last person she met with
before the wedding was me.

51:33.632 --> 51:34.466
What?

51:34.549 --> 51:35.383
[scoffs]

51:36.134 --> 51:38.845
I guess you didn't dig that deep.

51:38.929 --> 51:40.347
[mysterious music playing]

51:40.430 --> 51:41.556
[Hee-joo] When you two met,

51:42.682 --> 51:44.100
what did you talk about?

51:44.184 --> 51:45.310
[Sa-eon] We made a deal.

51:46.978 --> 51:48.021
[Hee-joo] What deal?

51:48.647 --> 51:50.065
Because of that deal,

51:50.148 --> 51:54.069
Hong In-a can never become
Paik Sa-eon's wife.

51:54.986 --> 51:56.112
What now?

51:56.822 --> 51:59.407
I think I just got rid of
your motive for blackmail.

51:59.908 --> 52:00.867
[phone snaps shut]

52:00.951 --> 52:02.077
[breathes heavily]

52:05.330 --> 52:06.748
He met with In-a?

52:07.290 --> 52:10.126
They made a deal? What deal?

52:11.253 --> 52:12.838
[door lock beeping]

52:16.132 --> 52:16.967
[door closes]

52:24.850 --> 52:25.934
[music ends]

52:26.935 --> 52:28.103
You're still up?

52:29.145 --> 52:32.566
I thought you'd be sleeping
after the stressful day you had today.

52:35.944 --> 52:38.613
I owe you an apology
for underestimating you.

52:39.906 --> 52:41.199
You did great.

52:44.160 --> 52:46.788
But the official results
haven't been announced yet.

52:46.872 --> 52:48.498
So don't get ahead of yourself.

52:51.001 --> 52:51.835
Also,

52:52.335 --> 52:55.463
I'm attending the Chungwoon Daily News
anniversary event tomorrow.

53:01.511 --> 53:02.804
[Hee-joo] Why all of a sudden?

53:03.680 --> 53:05.515
Do you know or not

53:06.474 --> 53:08.143
that my sister is back?

53:08.727 --> 53:10.854
You look beautiful. [chuckles]

53:13.148 --> 53:15.483
- [assistant] Hello.
- [Yeon-hui] Hi, so pretty.

53:15.567 --> 53:17.569
You know what day it is today, right?

53:17.652 --> 53:19.237
I want something special.

53:19.321 --> 53:20.739
Hello.

53:20.822 --> 53:21.698
[Yeon-hui] Hmm?

53:23.158 --> 53:24.326
Look who it is.

53:24.826 --> 53:25.994
Hello.

53:26.870 --> 53:27.913
Ms. Lee.

53:27.996 --> 53:30.332
Can you have two clients
in one room like this?

53:31.082 --> 53:33.084
[Ms. Lee] I'm sorry.
Show her to the waiting room.

53:37.631 --> 53:39.341
[Yeon-hui] We're a family.

53:40.842 --> 53:44.804
You're always so busy.
I didn't think you'd make it to the event.

53:44.888 --> 53:47.057
Just like last time,

53:47.140 --> 53:50.226
I thought your husband
would be coming with a cute aide.

54:05.951 --> 54:06.910
[scoffs]

54:07.661 --> 54:09.955
[sighs] I want my hair
to be higher than hers.

54:10.038 --> 54:11.748
Make my eyeliner wings longer too.

54:13.124 --> 54:14.042
[clears throat]

54:14.125 --> 54:16.670
CHUNGWOON DAILY NEWS
LEADING THE ERA, UNITING GENERATIONS

54:16.753 --> 54:18.630
CHUNGWOON CULTURAL FOUNDATION SCHOLARSHIP

54:18.713 --> 54:21.257
[classical music playing]

54:21.341 --> 54:23.301
CHUNGWOON
LEADING THE ERA, UNITING GENERATIONS

54:27.097 --> 54:28.640
[camera shutters clicking]

54:28.723 --> 54:30.392
[inaudible conversation]

54:33.687 --> 54:36.106
CHUNGWOON DAILY NEWS
70TH ANNIVERSARY CELEBRATION

54:36.189 --> 54:37.357
[Il-gyeong laughing]

54:37.440 --> 54:39.359
WITH THE PEOPLE
CHUNGWOON DAILY NEWS

54:39.442 --> 54:41.069
- Congratulations.
- [Il-gyeong] Thank you.

54:41.152 --> 54:43.196
[camera shutters clicking]

54:44.114 --> 54:46.866
[male MC] We'll begin
the cutting of the cake.

54:51.454 --> 54:52.706
[people applauding]

54:52.789 --> 54:54.666
[classical music continues playing]

55:08.471 --> 55:09.806
[mouthing]

55:13.101 --> 55:14.269
Congratulations.

55:14.936 --> 55:17.939
I wish you infinite success
and development in the future.

55:18.023 --> 55:19.691
Thank you so much.

55:19.774 --> 55:22.569
You're the busiest man in our country,
yet you made it.

55:22.652 --> 55:24.029
You flatter me. [laughs]

55:24.112 --> 55:26.823
We wouldn't miss
such a meaningful and joyous day.

55:26.906 --> 55:27.907
[exhales softly]

55:29.117 --> 55:29.951
But…

55:30.535 --> 55:32.370
I don't see our spokesperson yet.

55:35.081 --> 55:38.710
I wonder if the presidential office
is looking for a successor.

55:38.793 --> 55:41.212
If he wants to join
the presidential campaign,

55:41.963 --> 55:44.007
isn't it time he left his position?

55:44.090 --> 55:45.341
Of course.

55:46.217 --> 55:49.596
But as you know, he has so much ambition.

55:50.346 --> 55:53.058
I'm not sure
if he'll give up his career and join me.

55:53.725 --> 55:57.604
But still, I'll try harder
to convince him. [laughing]

55:58.396 --> 55:59.397
[laughing]

56:00.690 --> 56:03.526
How delightful. [laughing]

56:04.277 --> 56:05.111
Yes, okay.

56:05.862 --> 56:06.863
[elevator dings]

56:28.927 --> 56:29.886
[Yeon-hui] Hee-joo.

56:36.059 --> 56:37.977
Come with me.

56:41.189 --> 56:42.190
[elevator dings]

56:45.485 --> 56:46.694
[indistinct chatter]

56:59.499 --> 57:02.877
What's this about your dad?
The hospital called and said he was moved.

57:02.961 --> 57:03.795
Is that true?

57:09.050 --> 57:10.760
[Hee-joo] Your son-in-law moved him.

57:10.844 --> 57:12.011
[gasps]

57:12.095 --> 57:13.304
He did?

57:13.388 --> 57:16.850
Are you telling me
he found out about your dad?

57:18.518 --> 57:19.769
[exhales frustratingly]

57:19.853 --> 57:21.479
How could you let that happen?

57:21.563 --> 57:23.148
What if the chairman finds out?

57:24.941 --> 57:25.859
[sighs]

57:26.860 --> 57:30.363
Aren't you going to ask why he was moved
or what happened to him?

57:30.447 --> 57:31.448
[scoffs]

57:31.948 --> 57:32.824
I don't care.

57:32.907 --> 57:36.494
Anyway, now that he's been moved,
I don't need to pay anymore, right?

57:44.043 --> 57:45.044
That's much better.

57:46.880 --> 57:49.257
[door opens, closes]

57:49.340 --> 57:50.592
[woman] Did you see Sa-eon?

57:51.259 --> 57:53.136
He's in a whole different class now.

57:53.219 --> 57:54.929
I know, right?

57:55.013 --> 57:56.598
Is In-a not coming again today?

57:56.681 --> 57:59.642
She hasn't shown her face in public
since she got married.

58:00.310 --> 58:03.313
The president's daughter-in-law,
someone of great importance.

58:03.396 --> 58:04.314
Such a big deal.

58:05.231 --> 58:06.941
But In-a's sister is here.

58:07.025 --> 58:10.820
- She's such an attention-seeker.
- I always found her a bit off.

58:10.904 --> 58:13.823
She followed In-a around like a shadow.
So creepy.

58:14.532 --> 58:17.160
- Another glass of wine?
- Shall we? Let's go.

58:37.180 --> 58:38.932
[intriguing music playing]

58:39.516 --> 58:40.934
[indistinct chatter]

58:44.145 --> 58:45.146
[camera shutter clicks]

58:56.282 --> 58:58.159
[women laughing]

58:58.243 --> 58:59.202
[woman 1] Must be nice.

58:59.285 --> 59:01.287
- [woman 2] Let's toast.
- [woman 3] Cheers.

59:01.371 --> 59:02.205
[glasses clinking]

59:09.754 --> 59:11.506
[intriguing music continues playing]

59:25.562 --> 59:26.437
[sighs wearily]

59:45.790 --> 59:46.749
[music ends]

59:46.833 --> 59:48.001
[phone vibrating]

59:56.384 --> 59:57.594
[phone continues vibrating]

01:00:06.561 --> 01:00:09.188
CALLS
PAIK SA-EON

01:00:09.272 --> 01:00:11.274
[mellow music playing]

01:00:22.118 --> 01:00:22.952
PAIK SA-EON

01:00:23.036 --> 01:00:24.370
[line ringing]

01:00:41.471 --> 01:00:42.805
[line ringing]

01:00:56.903 --> 01:00:58.488
[inhales deeply]

01:00:58.571 --> 01:01:00.740
406, Hong Hee-joo.

01:01:02.909 --> 01:01:05.244
He must not care about either.

01:01:10.625 --> 01:01:11.751
[music fades]

01:01:11.834 --> 01:01:12.752
[Sa-eon] Hello?

01:01:17.215 --> 01:01:18.216
Speak.

01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:28.810
Your fiancée disappeared

01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:31.979
the day before the wedding,

01:01:33.856 --> 01:01:36.067
and Hong Hee-joo stepped in instead.

01:01:39.612 --> 01:01:40.905
How did you feel?

01:01:44.867 --> 01:01:46.494
Well, I get it.

01:01:46.577 --> 01:01:48.287
I'm sure it wasn't great.

01:01:51.666 --> 01:01:52.667
[Sa-eon] It was similar.

01:01:55.211 --> 01:01:56.212
[scoffs]

01:01:58.464 --> 01:01:59.298
Right.

01:02:00.550 --> 01:02:03.219
What use is she? Who else would take her?

01:02:04.011 --> 01:02:05.638
She's gloomy.

01:02:06.639 --> 01:02:08.808
She has no social skills.

01:02:10.518 --> 01:02:11.769
She's just…

01:02:15.189 --> 01:02:17.900
the supplementary pages
that came with Hong In-a.

01:02:17.984 --> 01:02:19.193
[slow music playing]

01:02:19.277 --> 01:02:20.111
Yeah.

01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:22.488
That's what she is.

01:02:22.572 --> 01:02:23.781
[chuckles softly]

01:02:24.282 --> 01:02:25.783
Do you know what's funnier?

01:02:26.367 --> 01:02:28.327
She always knew that too.

01:02:30.163 --> 01:02:33.666
But she hesitated each time
even though she wanted to break free.

01:02:34.250 --> 01:02:36.252
[indistinct chatter]

01:02:37.170 --> 01:02:39.213
[in distorted voice]
She didn't have the courage.

01:02:39.297 --> 01:02:42.175
She hated rich families
but was comforted by luxury.

01:02:43.009 --> 01:02:45.470
She cowardly succumbed to money.

01:02:57.523 --> 01:02:58.441
Hello?

01:03:03.154 --> 01:03:04.071
Hee-joo…

01:03:06.199 --> 01:03:07.533
isn't gloomy.

01:03:08.785 --> 01:03:10.787
She's observing her surroundings.

01:03:11.871 --> 01:03:13.456
She doesn't lack social skills.

01:03:14.749 --> 01:03:16.834
In general, people are rude to her first.

01:03:18.169 --> 01:03:20.963
- Also, she didn't succumb to money.
- [faint laughter]

01:03:23.007 --> 01:03:23.925
She just…

01:03:25.426 --> 01:03:26.969
loved her mother.

01:03:27.887 --> 01:03:29.889
[gripping music playing]

01:03:30.848 --> 01:03:31.849
There was a time

01:03:32.558 --> 01:03:36.312
when I hated to eat or speak
with my mouth.

01:03:37.688 --> 01:03:43.069
I was surrounded by greedy,
noisy, and bothersome people.

01:03:44.779 --> 01:03:46.280
And she was the most quiet.

01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:50.326
When I stared at her…

01:03:52.495 --> 01:03:54.580
strangely, I could breathe easily.

01:03:59.293 --> 01:04:00.294
What did you say?

01:04:01.003 --> 01:04:02.171
Supplementary pages?

01:04:02.255 --> 01:04:03.673
[scoffs]

01:04:03.756 --> 01:04:05.424
If you don't know, listen carefully, 406.

01:04:06.050 --> 01:04:07.885
Hee-joo isn't supplementary pages.

01:04:07.969 --> 01:04:09.762
She's a brand-new language.

01:04:10.429 --> 01:04:14.433
She's repeated the same hand movements
thousands of times to become who she is.

01:04:15.309 --> 01:04:16.769
People don't know that.

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:20.439
- So don't talk about my wife like that.
- [sobbing]

01:04:22.275 --> 01:04:25.278
[voice shaking] Then why did you treat her
like she was invisible?

01:04:27.530 --> 01:04:30.825
You say you know her so well.
Then why did you do that?

01:04:32.159 --> 01:04:34.954
Why did you tell her
not to think you were a couple?

01:04:36.122 --> 01:04:37.331
[elevator dings]

01:04:39.584 --> 01:04:41.586
[gripping music continues playing]

01:04:48.551 --> 01:04:49.635
[music fades]

01:04:58.311 --> 01:04:59.228
[scoffs]

01:04:59.312 --> 01:05:00.688
[dramatic music playing]

01:05:16.537 --> 01:05:19.457
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:05:19.540 --> 01:05:21.208
[officer 1] Okay, I'll take it now.

01:05:21.292 --> 01:05:24.003
- One, two, three!
- [camera shutter clicks]

01:05:24.086 --> 01:05:25.630
That was nice. One more.

01:05:25.713 --> 01:05:28.049
Wait. Can I shake your hand?

01:05:28.716 --> 01:05:30.217
- Of course.
- [officer 2 chuckles]

01:05:31.177 --> 01:05:34.055
[officer 1 chuckles] Okay.
One, two, three!

01:05:34.138 --> 01:05:35.181
[camera shutter clicks]

01:05:36.015 --> 01:05:38.017
- [Sa-eon exhales softly]
- Thank you so much.

01:05:38.100 --> 01:05:40.603
- [chuckles]
- [officer 1] It came out great.

01:05:41.312 --> 01:05:43.397
My wife will love this.

01:05:43.481 --> 01:05:44.899
- Sure.
- [officer 2 chuckles]

01:05:45.816 --> 01:05:48.361
Then, the report…

01:05:48.444 --> 01:05:49.320
That's right.

01:05:52.114 --> 01:05:52.990
[groans softly]

01:05:53.699 --> 01:05:54.825
I almost forgot.

01:05:54.909 --> 01:05:57.328
Is your wife okay?

01:05:57.995 --> 01:05:59.413
[chuckles nervously] Thanks to you.

01:05:59.497 --> 01:06:01.749
Thank you for your concern.

01:06:01.832 --> 01:06:03.292
We're relieved to hear it.

01:06:03.376 --> 01:06:06.253
She was so shocked that day.

01:06:06.337 --> 01:06:08.839
I thought she was having a panic attack.

01:06:10.216 --> 01:06:11.801
A panic attack?

01:06:11.884 --> 01:06:12.927
Yes.

01:06:13.010 --> 01:06:16.097
She was like… [retching]

01:06:16.180 --> 01:06:17.264
Her face got so pale.

01:06:17.348 --> 01:06:20.309
She was screaming so loudly too.

01:06:20.393 --> 01:06:22.311
We were on the road then,

01:06:22.395 --> 01:06:24.230
but I pulled over and let her out.

01:06:24.313 --> 01:06:26.983
It would've been bad
if we hadn't. [chuckles]

01:06:27.566 --> 01:06:28.401
[Sa-eon] Wait.

01:06:30.111 --> 01:06:31.904
What did you just say?

01:06:33.280 --> 01:06:34.115
What?

01:06:36.033 --> 01:06:36.993
Well…

01:06:39.328 --> 01:06:41.580
- A panic…
- No, not that.

01:06:44.333 --> 01:06:46.335
She screamed?

01:06:48.129 --> 01:06:49.088
My wife did?

01:06:49.171 --> 01:06:51.173
[gripping music playing]

01:06:58.264 --> 01:07:00.141
What is it? What's wrong?

01:07:00.850 --> 01:07:03.185
- What…
- [officer 1] Are you feeling sick?

01:07:03.269 --> 01:07:04.895
[Hee-joo sobbing]

01:07:05.646 --> 01:07:06.981
[Hee-joo] Let me out.

01:07:09.775 --> 01:07:11.694
Let me out. [breathing heavily]

01:07:11.777 --> 01:07:13.738
We're on the road right now.

01:07:13.821 --> 01:07:15.698
It'll be okay if you just let me out.

01:07:15.781 --> 01:07:17.575
It'll be okay, so let me out!

01:07:17.658 --> 01:07:19.493
[screaming] Please, let me out!

01:07:19.577 --> 01:07:21.203
[indistinct conversation]

01:07:21.704 --> 01:07:22.913
[Hee-joo breathing heavily]

01:07:22.997 --> 01:07:24.999
[gripping music continues playing]

01:07:41.807 --> 01:07:44.101
[Hee-joo] I can't do this.
Just let me out.

01:07:46.520 --> 01:07:48.856
[breathing heavily] Just let me out.

01:07:51.108 --> 01:07:53.235
[engine revving]

01:07:54.820 --> 01:07:56.614
Please, let me out!

01:07:56.697 --> 01:07:58.199
[tires screech]

01:08:03.913 --> 01:08:04.914
[music ends]

01:08:05.539 --> 01:08:07.541
[dramatic song playing]

01:08:08.125 --> 01:08:08.959
[scoffs]

01:08:12.963 --> 01:08:13.798
[scoffs]

01:08:21.764 --> 01:08:22.598
[scoffs]

01:08:56.632 --> 01:08:59.552
WHEN THE PHONE RINGS

01:09:01.387 --> 01:09:02.555
Why did you go that far?

01:09:03.305 --> 01:09:06.058
[Hee-joo] Don't you have any?
Something you're hiding from me.

01:09:06.142 --> 01:09:07.434
[scoffs]

01:09:07.518 --> 01:09:10.271
This is great for Hee-joo!
She's going to the presidential office.

01:09:10.354 --> 01:09:14.150
[Sa-eon] What's a good gift
to give someone who just got a job?

01:09:15.860 --> 01:09:18.320
I look forward to working with you.

01:09:19.280 --> 01:09:20.698
[Do-jae] Don't be surprised.

01:09:20.781 --> 01:09:21.991
406 is…

01:09:22.074 --> 01:09:23.492
- [Sa-eon] A woman?
- Paik Sa-eon!

01:09:23.576 --> 01:09:24.743
[car accelerating]

01:09:26.620 --> 01:09:28.247
[tires screech]

01:09:32.376 --> 01:09:34.378
Subtitle translation by: Sue Mounce
